{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>For some positive real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/77500eaad809c17abfb6f78eeff713aa02d7e61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5e07b1eb38899818af2d6cfe23256530693547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f65450756c44b33df63c304f031fdfc2751a0d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />, and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c110affda889ec527f09bd00cb3ebb3beb0be818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DAC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f0c875afc1b7d809b7f9c321a296e6a800f7ae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4t$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />. If the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/848ec5b5f695afbacb864efead154761481780c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, what is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7fb67ee1591d09e7bd35703ca876d209a96efed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 168 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 105 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 84 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 189 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 126$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"470\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the diagram, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is made up of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5e07b1eb38899818af2d6cfe23256530693547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. Using the areas, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3103fa45f42bde3688b087d515921b81021c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t + 2t = 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/6387fa2ab196f208fc4b5c85eb53b0e769537609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3t = 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6ddee1afcd08d26126058a42ee10f26b396ecb34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\frac{63}{3} = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is made up of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/77500eaad809c17abfb6f78eeff713aa02d7e61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fbf0a38e6a867c8db4c2477c657c234699d1b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ABC] = [\\triangle DEC] + [\\triangle DBE] + \\triangle [ADC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15fd3127582e488e50ec1aae4bab2916945c9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=63 + t + 4t = 63 + 5t = 63 + 5 \\times 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"300\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8dd181e40fdd2a906aa61f3ef0ac4c7970aada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=63 + 105 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 168}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"187\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9